But the test output message: "UNIQUE constraint failed: certificados.codigo" with code "SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_PRIMARYKEY". So I'll match on `code === 'SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_PRIMARYKEY'`. Should I also match `SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_UNIQUE`? If there were a UNIQUE index on codigo instead of PK, code would be SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_UNIQUE. But since it's PK, the code is PRIMARYKEY. The task explicitly says "violação de unicidade/PRIMARY KEY de certificados.codigo". To be safe and explicit, I'll match both `SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_PRIMARYKEY` and `SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_UNIQUE` — but ONLY when the message references `codigo`. Hmm, that adds message parsing coupling.

