But there's a subtlety: each retry regenerates the whole `certificado` object — code changes, but the rest are the same. I can generate just the code per attempt and reuse the rest of fields, or construct per attempt. Cleanest: build the static parts once, and per-attempt only the codigo differs. But simpler to construct the object inside the loop. Either is fine. I'll build once and only change codigo:

